STEP 2: In live session terminal:
    sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y gparted
    sudo e2fsck -f /dev/nvme0n1p6
    sudo e2fsck -f /dev/nvme0n1p4

  STEP 3:
    sudo gparted /dev/nvme0n1
    - Right-click partition 4 (/data, ext4) -> Delete
    - Right-click partition 6 (/, ext4) -> Resize/Move -> drag left edge all the way left -> Resize/Move
    - Apply All Operations (confirm)
    - Wait for it to finish (NVMe, expect ~5-20 min)

  STEP 4: Fix fstab from live session (if not already commented out):
    sudo mkdir -p /mnt/root
    sudo mount /dev/nvme0n1p6 /mnt/root
    sudo nano /mnt/root/etc/fstab      # remove/comment the /data line
    sudo umount /mnt/root

  STEP 5: Remove USB, reboot normally, verify:
    df -h /
    # should show ~465G single root partition

  Cleanup after confirming all is well:
    rmdir /data

